# Data and API Contracts

- PostgreSQL is the source of truth. Schema changes only via migrations.
- Repositories own SQL access. Handlers never embed SQL.
- Version all REST endpoints under `/api/v1`.
- Shared DTOs live in `packages/types` when consumed by web.
- Calendar and other integrations use provider interfaces from day one (Google first).
- Login identity ≠ integration connection. Store connections separately.
- Validate all inbound API input. Never trust the frontend.
